## The authored sweep

The thirty desks run through sky records; Greek explanation and ethical inquiry; Plato and Aristotle’s kinds; Cynics, Stoics, Epicureans and sceptics; mathematical and textual models; translation and active commentary; optics; medieval disputation; print and editions; perspective and maps; moving-Earth astronomy; Bacon and practical inquiry; mechanism and gravitation; longitude and observatories; public knowledge and rights; exchange and work; geological time; evolution; the costs of progress; microorganisms and disease; fields, clocks and photography; experience and Surrealism; relativity; Earth’s measurable age and plate tectonics; computation; Borges and reproduction; critical histories of categories; planetary science; and two explicitly speculative future desks.

Dates are local and overlapping files explicitly say so. This is not a claim that every earlier idea caused the next. Cross-links distinguish transmission, adaptation, criticism, modern teaching comparison and future speculation.

Representative substantive returns include:

- A record of eclipse recurrence becomes a physical explanatory question, not a more elaborate arithmetic exercise.
- A counterexample about returning a weapon reopens the definition of justice; a distinct subsequent creation opens the wider examined-life question.
- A fixed viewpoint’s hidden surfaces constrain what a photograph can establish.
- Deep geological time lets cumulative selection matter; later isotope clocks answer the separate unresolved numerical-age question.
- Wegener’s evidence can be persuasive while his driving mechanism remains inadequate; later ocean-floor evidence earns a different plate framework.
- Patterson’s contamination problem connects measurement of the ancient Earth to industrial lead in the modern world.
- An exact textual comparison finds the same words in Borges’s invented Menard case; changed attribution then changes the reading.
- Future automation retains the distinct obligations of useful work, maker agency and care. Rapid response and contestability remain in tension at the ending.

## Intended feel and limits

Current scenes begin with **8–17 tangible tiles** and reach at most **29** on the full author route. Earlier creations are carried only when used locally. Sources and rival claims stay live; physical ingredients are transformed or incorporated only at explicit events. There is no finite-scarcity puzzle, compulsory calculation, hidden diagram or arbitrary finished-item culling. Every tile has deliberate optional Read context; labels must still do the primary work.

These are authoring intentions and logical facts, not a claim that real players find every operation intuitive. The v2 readers identified several near-renaming gates and some weak Read context. The bounded v3 repair removes those gates and gives returning ideas specific work without shrinking the requested richness or demoting ordinary highlighting. No indefinite simulated-fun iteration was performed.

